course: dictionary
lesson: 1252
title: Burglary: a crime and a single event
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Burglary is a noun, and it can mean two things. It is the crime of breaking into a building to steal things. It can also mean one single time this happens: «There was a burglary next door.» Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Context helps you spot the meaning. «A burglary is when someone breaks into a home to steal; victims are often upset most by feeling unsafe.» The sentence tells you the crime is about breaking in and stealing, and that it can leave people feeling scared.
explain: Be careful with clues that seem to point at a person. «Police at a door can mean a burglary, an accident, bad news or someone needing help; it never proves that a person did wrong.» A police officer at the door does not prove a burglary has happened. Check all the other words before you decide.
fact: Burglary is the crime of breaking into a building to steal things.
fact: A burglary is one time this crime happens: «There was a burglary next door.»
fact: A burglar is the person who commits a burglary, and burgle is the verb.
fact: A burglar alarm warns people when someone breaks in.
fact: When something bad happens to someone, like a burglary, the blame belongs to the person who did it, not the person it happened to.
exercise: «The burglary happened while the family was on holiday.» What does burglary mean here? | A loud noise made by a car | A family holiday by the sea | A visit from a friendly neighbour | *Breaking into a building to steal things
exercise: Ayesha says, «A police car outside means a burglary for sure.» Is she right? | Yes, police only come when a burglary is happening | *No, police at a door can mean many things, and it never proves someone did wrong | Yes, and the burglar is still inside | No, police at a door can mean an accident, bad news or someone needing help
exercise: Which word means the person who commits a burglary? | *Burglar | Burglary | Burgle | Alarm
test: After a burglary, who is to blame? | The person it happened to | The police | *The person who did it | Nobody, it is just bad luck
test: «It is scary because home should feel safe, and the feeling of being unsafe fades with time and safety steps like new locks.» What helps a home feel safe again? | Forgetting about it | Inviting strangers in | Leaving doors open | *New locks and safety steps
exam: «2 burglaries becoming 3 is a rise of 50%, but it is only one more burglary.» What is the real change in the number of burglaries? | A rise of 50 burglaries | *Only one more burglary | Two burglaries less | Burglary became a happy word
